base access, input validation, JSON encoding into testable functions with clear error handling. Keep external behavior identical: same status codes, same response bodies. Need full refactored file. Need likely define sentinel errors: ErrInvalidID, ErrUserNotFound, ErrDatabase? But external behavior: 400 body {\"error\":\"bad id\"} no Content-Type? Original 400/404/500 do not set Content-Type. Success sets Content-Type application/json and encodes map. JSON encoder adds newline. Need preserve exact bodies? \"same response bodies\" likely exact bytes. For success, json.Encoder.Encode(map[string]string{\"name\": name, \"email\": email}) produces {\"email\":\"...\",\"name\":\"...\"}\\n because Go map keys sorted alphabetically. Need preserve. If we use json.Marshal(map[string]string{...}) no newline. Need use json.NewEncoder(w).Encode or write exact. To keep identical, use json.NewEncoder(w).Encode(user) where user struct? If", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0037658701185137033], [760, -6.621825218200684]], [[1144, -1.3709161976294126e-05], [14235, -12.107841491699219]], [[4087, -0.010781984776258469], [310, -4.725961208343506]], [[1156, -0.03342499956488609], [303, -3.692021131515503]], [[579, -0.2386743724346161], [25, -2.2894861698150635]], [[1622, -0.0035862780641764402], [3296, -6.407289981842041]], [[13, -0.33834192156791687], [25, -1.6186572313308716]], [[14235, -0.03660624846816063], [1165, -4.033562183380127]], [[89109, -0.32706454396247864], [7936, -1.8199883699417114]], [[5805, -0.0002586579939816147], [2400, -8.66126537322998]], [[9830, -0.024098802357912064], [6795, -3.7893080711364746]], [[6795, -2.908749047492165e-05], [17369, -11.893095016479492]], [[1083, -1.3929810523986816], [47781, -1.571413516998291]], [[1228, -0.0891367495059967], [2400, -2.871931552886963]], [[470, -3.0637256713816896e-05], [5568, -10.658159255981445]], [[5568, -0.002891185926273465], [74243, -6.190810680389404]], [[440, -0.8841028809547424], [25, -1.9052457809448242]], [[2708, -0.0352216064